  "result": "Perfect! All 83 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added discount support:\n- `isValidDiscount()` validates discounts are numbers between 0\u2013100 (decimals allowed)\n- **`createInvoice`** now accepts `discountPercent` in each line input\n- **`addLine`** now accepts `discountPercent` parameter\n- **`lineDiscount(line)`** \u2014 Returns discount amount = `lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100` (rounded, clamped at 0)\n- **`invoiceTotals(invoice)`** \u2014 Returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }`:\n  - `subtotal` = sum of undiscounted line totals\n  - `discount` = sum of all line discounts\n  - `total` = `subtotal - discount` (clamped at 0)\n\n**src/render.js** \u2014 Updated to show discounts:\n- Lines with discounts render as: `qty \u00d7 name @ unitPrice = lineTotal - discount = netTotal`\n- Invoices with any discounts show:\n  ```\n  Subtotal: \u20acX.XX\n  Discount: -\u20acY.YY\n  Total: \u20acZ.ZZ\n  ```\n\n**Tests** \u2014 16 new tests covering:\n- Discount validation (range, type, decimals)\n- `lineDiscount` calculation (with and without discount, decimal percentages)\n- `invoiceTotals` with discounts, including clamping at 0\n- `addLine` with `discountPercent` parameter\n- Rendering discounts on individual lines\n- Subtotal/discount lines in output\n\nAll 83 tests pass \u2713",
